# The settings of the service under `docker compose up`. Copy this file to `.env.memini` next to
# compose.yaml and uncomment what you need; `.env.memini` is ignored by git. Compose passes every
# line into the service's container as it is (MEMINI_ENV_FILE in .env names another file), so a
# setting needs no change of compose.yaml. Every line is optional: without the file, the service
# runs with its defaults, and with them no embeddings. After a change: `docker compose up -d`.
#
# docs/configuration.md describes each setting and what a change of it needs. A value shown here is
# the default, so uncommenting a line as it is changes nothing, unless the line says otherwise.
#
# Never put a secret here: these values show in `docker inspect`. Keys and tokens go into files
# that .env names (MEMINI_CREDENTIAL_KEY_FILE and the others in .env.example), and so do the ssh key
# and known_hosts of git. Compose itself sets the database URL, MEMINI_HTTP_HOST, MEMINI_HTTP_PORT,
# MEMINI_GIT_MIRROR_DIR and the variables of those files: a line for one of them here has no
# effect. Values are read as compose reads .env: `#` after a space starts a comment, and a value can
# be quoted.

# --- Logs and operator ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CRITICAL, ERROR, WARNING, INFO or DEBUG.
# MEMINI_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
#
# Seconds a database statement may take before it is logged as slow (without its parameters);
# 0 turns the slow-statement log off.
# MEMINI_LOG_SLOW_STATEMENT_THRESHOLD=1.0
#
# The principal the operator commands act as (`memini bootstrap` gives it the first admin token).
# Keep it the same after the first bootstrap.
# MEMINI_PRINCIPAL=owner

# --- Embeddings ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Off until a provider is set. Without embeddings the service starts and serves, but it does not
# sync git sources, and search answers that no embedding provider is configured (read_source
# works).
#
# The default model is Qwen3-Embedding 0.6B, served by Ollama on the host (docs/requirements.md,
# open question 2). To turn it on:
#
#   1. Install Ollama on the host and pull the model (about 640 MB):
#        ollama pull qwen3-embedding:0.6b
#   2. Uncomment the provider and the URL below, then `docker compose up -d`.
#
# Inside the container 127.0.0.1 is the container itself, so the URL, Ollama on the host, is needed
# with the provider; the rest follows from the provider. On Linux, Ollama listens on 127.0.0.1
# only, which a container cannot reach. Let it listen on the Docker bridge as well, e.g.
# `OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0:11434` in its systemd unit, and keep port 11434 closed to other machines with
# a firewall. Docker Desktop and OrbStack reach the host's 127.0.0.1 through host.docker.internal
# without that.

# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1

# The provider implies the settings below; they are listed to show what is pinned. Set one only to
# change it. Changing the URL needs nothing else; changing the model, the dimension, the digest or
# the document prefix changes the index fingerprint, and search stays refused until
# `memini reindex` rebuilds each workspace.
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible /v1/embeddings API works as the URL (llama.cpp, vLLM); a cloud endpoint gets
# your text, so choose it on purpose. Its key, if it needs one: MEMINI_EMBEDDING_API_KEY_FILE in
# .env.
#
# The model, its vector size and the digest of the Ollama build the eval measured (Q8_0, as
# `ollama list` shows its first 12 digits). The digest is recorded in the index fingerprint and
# is not checked against Ollama: after `ollama pull` brings a new build, set its digest here and
# reindex. Another model needs its own dimension, and gets no digest or query instruction.
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=qwen3-embedding:0.6b
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_DIMENSION=1024
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_DIGEST=ac6da0dfba84a81fdbfbaf330198c33cd77c4cdfc53e8bc50eb581914a15621d
#
# Qwen3-Embedding puts an instruction before each query and none before documents. In a
# double-quoted value compose turns \n into a line break. Changing the query prefix needs no
# reindex.
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_QUERY_PREFIX="Instruct: Given a search query, retrieve the relevant code or documentation that can help answer the query\nQuery:"
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_DOCUMENT_PREFIX=
#
# Texts per request and seconds per request.
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_BATCH_SIZE=32
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_TIMEOUT=60
#
# The `local` provider is not set up in the image: it has the runtime of in-process models, for the
# reranker below, but no embedding model and no writable place for one.

# --- Git connector -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Seconds a clone or fetch may take; the largest mirror on disk, and the largest file read from one.
# MEMINI_GIT_FETCH_TIMEOUT=600
# MEMINI_GIT_MAX_MIRROR_SIZE=5G
# MEMINI_GIT_MAX_BLOB_SIZE=1M
#
# Allow plain http:// remotes, without TLS.
# MEMINI_GIT_ALLOW_HTTP=false
#
# Restricted HTTPS Git for delegated administrators. Configure the proxy ACL and address pins
# as in docs/security.md. With the proxy enabled, an empty origin list denies network Git.
# MEMINI_GIT_EGRESS_PROXY=http://git-proxy:3128
# MEMINI_GIT_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
#
# Local repositories as sources: directories in the container, comma-separated, e.g. /srv/repos.
# Each must be mounted into the container as well: compose.yaml has an example under `volumes`.
# MEMINI_GIT_LOCAL_ROOTS=
#
# The token for https remotes is a file (.env.example). The hosts it may be sent to, comma-separated,
# e.g. github.com: required with the token. The user name sent with it.
# MEMINI_GIT_HTTPS_TOKEN_HOSTS=
# MEMINI_GIT_HTTPS_USERNAME=x-access-token

# --- MCP service executor ------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The MCP servers mcp sources may reach, comma-separated: host names (mcp.example.com, host:port,
# *.example.com) or URL prefixes (https://mcp.example.com/v1). Empty: none.
# MEMINI_MCP_ALLOWED_ENDPOINTS=
#
# Internal networks (CIDR) an endpoint may resolve to all the same, e.g. 172.17.0.0/16 for a server
# on the host under compose. Empty: none; loopback, private and link-local addresses are refused.
# MEMINI_MCP_ALLOWED_NETWORKS=
#
# Allow plain http:// MCP endpoints, without TLS.
# MEMINI_MCP_ALLOW_HTTP=false
#
# Executables in the container mcp sources may run as stdio servers, by absolute path.
# MEMINI_MCP_ALLOWED_COMMANDS=
# Exact stdio command, arguments and optional credential variable (JSON array).
# MEMINI_MCP_ALLOWED_INVOCATIONS=[]
#
# Tries of one call of an mcp sync, the first included.
# MEMINI_MCP_CALL_ATTEMPTS=3

# --- Search --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Seconds one search statement may run; candidates per retriever of a hybrid search; the k of
# reciprocal rank fusion, and the weight of each retriever's ranks in it.
# MEMINI_SEARCH_TIMEOUT=5
# MEMINI_SEARCH_CANDIDATES=50
# MEMINI_SEARCH_RRF_K=1
# MEMINI_SEARCH_DENSE_WEIGHT=3
# MEMINI_SEARCH_LEXICAL_WEIGHT=1
#
# Reranking of the best hits by Qwen3-Reranker 0.6B in the process (docs/requirements.md, section 9,
# Reranker): on in the image, which carries its runtime and its model files (about 610 MB; see
# MEMINI_RERANKER_FILES in .env), verified against the digest at each start. It reorders the best
# 3 hits of a search: on the code suite hybrid R@1 goes from 0.61 to 0.77. It adds 0.5 to 0.7 s to
# a search on 4 CPUs, 1.2 s on 2 and 2.2 s on 1, and the service holds about 1 GB more. Until
# the model is loaded, a few seconds after the start, and if it cannot load, search keeps the
# fused order. none turns it off.
# MEMINI_SEARCH_RERANKER=local
# MEMINI_SEARCH_RERANK_DEPTH=3
#
# The model and its files. Another model needs its own digest and revision, and a writable
# directory for its files, such as a volume: the image's /opt/memini/models is read-only.
# MEMINI_SEARCH_RERANKER_MODEL=n24q02m/Qwen3-Reranker-0.6B-ONNX
# MEMINI_SEARCH_RERANKER_MODEL_FILE=onnx/model_yesno_quantized.onnx
# MEMINI_SEARCH_RERANKER_DIGEST=sha256:eaa6edfadd2440e4f80851b3ff7701f26e8ec6aacaa2fedcee8ce86afd09afea
# MEMINI_SEARCH_RERANKER_REVISION=342a8a54de23bba03eb8cce5f5bef503edf18315
# MEMINI_SEARCH_RERANKER_MODEL_DIR=/opt/memini/models
#
# Tokens of one query and hit; seconds one search's reranking may take before the search keeps the
# fused order; threads of one model run (0: as many as the CPUs, or a CPU limit set with `cpus` in
# compose.yaml, allow, at most 4).
# MEMINI_SEARCH_RERANKER_MAX_TOKENS=1024
# MEMINI_SEARCH_RERANKER_TIMEOUT=5
# MEMINI_SEARCH_RERANKER_THREADS=0

# --- Ingest and retention ------------------------------------------------------------------------

# One batch sent to the ingest API: its body, its records, and the payload of one record as stored.
# The body size also bounds a raw response an agent run's capture hook posts.
# MEMINI_INGEST_MAX_BODY_SIZE=16M
# MEMINI_INGEST_MAX_RECORDS=1000
# MEMINI_INGEST_MAX_PAYLOAD_SIZE=1M
#
# Seconds between two retention passes over a source that has retention_days, and records one
# transaction of a pass deletes at most.
# MEMINI_RETENTION_INTERVAL=3600
# MEMINI_RETENTION_BATCH_SIZE=1000

# --- Request limits ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Limits of every HTTP and MCP request (docs/requirements.md, section 7). The largest body outside
# the ingest and raw response routes (bytes, or with K, M or G), and seconds a database statement of
# a request may run and its transaction may stay idle (0: the database's default).
# MEMINI_HTTP_MAX_BODY_SIZE=1M
# MEMINI_HTTP_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT=30
# MEMINI_HTTP_IDLE_IN_TRANSACTION_TIMEOUT=300
#
# Requests a minute: per token, reads (GET, and MCP requests) and writes (POST, PUT, PATCH,
# DELETE, and MCP calls of write tools such as record_decision); per client address, requests whose
# token is not known to be valid. false turns rate limits off.
# MEMINI_HTTP_RATE_LIMIT=true
# MEMINI_HTTP_RATE_LIMIT_READS=600
# MEMINI_HTTP_RATE_LIMIT_WRITES=120
# MEMINI_HTTP_RATE_LIMIT_UNAUTHENTICATED=60

# --- LLM providers -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# None by default, and then nothing is extracted. At most two OpenAI-compatible chat APIs, declared
# by the slot they are set in: local is trusted with the content of every source, cloud (https
# only) only with sources whose llm_policy is cloud, in workspaces that opted in. Each slot needs
# its URL and its model; the URL and the model below are examples, not defaults. Their keys, if they
# need any: MEMINI_LLM_LOCAL_API_KEY_FILE and MEMINI_LLM_CLOUD_API_KEY_FILE in .env.
# MEMINI_LLM_LOCAL_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# MEMINI_LLM_LOCAL_MODEL=the-model-name
# MEMINI_LLM_LOCAL_STRUCTURED_OUTPUT=json_schema
# MEMINI_LLM_CLOUD_URL=https://llm.example.com/v1
# MEMINI_LLM_CLOUD_MODEL=the-model-name
# MEMINI_LLM_CLOUD_STRUCTURED_OUTPUT=json_schema
#
# Seconds per LLM request; only with a provider.
# MEMINI_LLM_TIMEOUT=300

# --- Decision extraction -------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Only with an LLM provider: each new or changed thread or meeting gets an extraction job. Active
# items a new item is checked against for duplicates, replacements and answers, and how they are
# found: by words (lexical), or by words and statement vectors (hybrid; needs an embedding provider).
# MEMINI_EXTRACTION_CANDIDATES=8
# MEMINI_EXTRACTION_CANDIDATE_RETRIEVER=hybrid
